<title>CANADA: AGREEMENT REACHED IN BRITISH COLUMBIA LUMBER TALKS.</title>
<headline>AGREEMENT REACHED IN BRITISH COLUMBIA LUMBER TALKS.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Columbia's coastal forest companies  and the lumber workers union reached agreement on Friday on a new  three-year labor contract, a negotiator for the companies said.</p>
<p>&quot;We're very pleased. We were able to reach an agreement with the IWA  (union),&quot; said Keith Bennett, chief negotiator for Forest Industrial  Relations, which bargains for 65 forestry companies in the west coast  Canadian province.</p>
<p>Bennett said the three-year deal provided for wage increases of one  percent in the first year and two percent in each of the subsequent  years.</p>
</text>
